# oracle: pair lj/long/dipole/long cut long 2.5 (cut LJ, long-range dipoles) with kspace_style ewald/disp/dipole 1e-4 and no charges: the Coulomb term is dropped and G-ewald comes from the Newton solve of the dipole real-space error (Wang-Holm), 108 fcc point dipoles 0.7, fix nve/sphere update dipole, 20 steps, final torques compared.
# oracle-files: w211ed_dipole_only_tq.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 filerel=1e-8
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.3e-13, atoms 1.9e-15.
units           lj
atom_style      hybrid sphere dipole
boundary        p p p
lattice         fcc 0.4
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
set             group all diameter 1.0
set             group all density 1.0
set             group all dipole/random 4421 0.7
velocity        all create 1.0 87287 dist gaussian
pair_style      lj/long/dipole/long cut long 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0
kspace_style    ewald/disp/dipole 1.0e-4
fix             1 all nve/sphere update dipole
timestep        0.002
thermo_style    custom step temp pe evdwl ecoul elong press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          10
run             20
write_dump      all custom w211ed_dipole_only_tq.dump id tqx tqy tqz modify format float %.15g sort id
